---
import { REPO_URL } from "../lib/release";

const QUARANTINE = "xattr -dr com.apple.quarantine /Applications/Sikemux.app";
---

<section class="section" id="faq">
    <div class="page grid">
        <div class="section-head">
            <p class="label">Questions</p>
            <h2>Before you download.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="list">
            <details>
                <summary>Is this Electron?</summary>
                <p>
                    No. It's Tauri 2 with a Rust backend. Shells are native PTYs owned by Rust, and the interface is React running in the
                    system WebView, so there's no bundled Chromium.
                </p>
            </details>
            <details>
                <summary>Which agents does it work with?</summary>
                <p>
                    Claude Code, Codex, Hermes, Pi and OpenCode. Sikemux finds them on your <code>PATH</code> and launches them through your
                    own shell, so they get your environment and your login.
                </p>
            </details>
            <details>
                <summary>Does Sikemux send my code to a model?</summary>
                <p>
                    No. It has no model and needs no API key. When it writes a commit message, it asks the CLI you pick, which uses its own
                    login.
                </p>
            </details>
            <details>
                <summary>macOS says it can't check the app for malware.</summary>
                <p>Builds aren't notarized by Apple yet. Drag Sikemux into Applications, then run this once:</p>
                <pre><code>{QUARANTINE}</code></pre>
                <p>After that, updates install from inside the app.</p>
            </details>
            <details>
                <summary>Intel Macs, Windows, Linux?</summary>
                <p>
                    Published builds are Apple Silicon only, on macOS 11 or later. A Windows installer builds from source today, but there's no
                    Windows download yet. There's no Linux build.
                </p>
            </details>
            <details>
                <summary>What does it cost?</summary>
                <p>Nothing. It's MIT licensed, and the <a href={REPO_URL}>source is on GitHub</a>.</p>
            </details>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<style>
    .grid {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 2fr);
        gap: clamp(24px, 5vw, 72px);
    }

    .list {
        border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    }

    details {
        border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    }

    summary {
        display: flex;
        align-items: center;
        justify-content: space-between;
        gap: 16px;
        padding-block: 18px;
        font-size: 16px;
        font-weight: 500;
        color: var(--text-primary);
        cursor: pointer;
        list-style: none;
    }

    summary::-webkit-details-marker {
        display: none;
    }

    summary::after {
        content: "+";
        font-family: var(--mono);
        font-weight: 400;
        color: var(--text-tertiary);
        transition: transform var(--dur-2) var(--ease-out);
    }

    details[open] summary::after {
        transform: rotate(45deg);
    }

    details p {
        max-width: 62ch;
        padding-bottom: 14px;
    }

    details p:last-child {
        padding-bottom: 20px;
    }

    details a {
        color: var(--acc);
        text-decoration: underline;
        text-underline-offset: 3px;
    }

    pre {
        margin: 0 0 14px;
        padding: 12px 14px;
        border: 1px solid var(--border);
        border-radius: var(--radius-2);
        background: var(--surface);
        overflow-x: auto;
        font-size: 13px;
        color: var(--text-primary);
    }

    pre code {
        font-size: inherit;
    }

    @media (max-width: 860px) {
        .grid {
            grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
        }
    }
</style>
